    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d268-a6">

                <pb facs="0487" n="1447" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1447"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 6 in No.
                    272.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. de la Torre to Mr. Williams.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Office of the Collector of Customs</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Havana</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1887-12-06"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 6, 1887</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In reply to your attentive letter of the
                    5th instant, I have the honor to inform you that Spanish vessels arriving here
                    from Porto Rico in ballast and sailing afterward loaded with sugar for the
                    United States pay tonnage dues at the rate of 25 cents for <pb facs="0488"
                        n="1448" xml:id="pg1448"/> each thousand kilos, gross, excepting those
                    Spanish steamers of periodical trips, which enjoy an exemption from their
                    payment.</p>
                <p>The tonnage dues collected in Porto Rico do not serve as a basis at all in this
                    island, because of the different manner in which they are collected.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alfonso de la
                    Torre.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
